==Ainu==
{{rfc|ain}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ain-IPA|án}}

===Etymology 1===
Possibly a [[shortened]] form of ''[[anihi]]''. It may also have come directly from the verb ''[[an]]'' (to [[be]], to [[exist]]).

===Pronominal Sufix===
{{ain-pron|l|{{ain-kana-conv|アン}}}}

# {{lb|ain|intransitive indefinite pronominal affix}}  [[someone]], [[somebody]]. An undetermined or unspecified [[person]] or [[thing]]. It can also refer to someone whose identity is clear from the context.
#: {{syn|ain|a|sinuma|asinuma|anihi}}
#: {{uxa|ain|Cis-'''an'''.|'''Someone''' is crying.}}
#: {{uxa|ain|Asinuma akar sinot-'''an'''.|'''We'''’re playing.}}
#: {{uxa|ain|Pirka-'''an'''.|'''You’re''' beautiful.}}
#: {{uxa|ain|Aynu ray-'''an'''.|'''The person''' is dying.}}

===Usage notes===
*'''-an''', no matter the context, is only used with [[intransitive]] verbs.
*'''-an''' may act as an [[emphasizing]] pronoun, emphasizing what is doing the action. This may lead to situations where the context is ambiguous, since the verb could be in the passive voice. In example four, it can mean “'''The person''' is dying” or “'''The person is being killed'''.”
* '''-an''' may be often used as an [[inclusive]] first-person pronoun ([[we]]) as well as a [[respectful]] second-person pronoun. See examples two and three.
* As for [[transitive]] verbs, [[a|a-]] should be used instead.

===Etymology 2===
Similar to {{cog|ja|-}} {{ja-r|ある}}.

===Affix===
{{ain-verb|l|{{ain-kana-conv|アン}}}}

# {{lb|ain|suffix}} Used with [[inalienable]] nouns to show either [[quality]] or [[possessiveness]].
#: {{ant|ain|sak}}
#: {{usex|ain|[[kamuy|Kamuy]] '''kiror’an''' cikoykip ne.|Bears are '''strong''' animals (lit. Bears are animals that '''have strengh''').}}

===Verb===
{{ain-verb|l|{{ain-kana-conv|アン}}|okay|ante}}

# {{lb|ain|intransitive|stative}} to [[exist]], [[be]] (somewhere); [[there is]].
#: {{ant|ain|isam}}
#: {{usex|ain|Aynu '''an''' [[ruwe ne]].|'''There is''' an Ainu.}}
# {{lb|ain|intransitive|only when used with inalienable nouns}} to [[have]].
#: {{ant|ain|isam}}
#: {{usex|ain|An aynu sine paraure ka '''an'''.|Some people only '''have''' one leg.}}
# {{lb|ain|intransitive|stative|continuative}} (As of states, often used after [[wa]]) to [[stay]], to [[keep]], to be [[still]] (doing something).
#: {{ant|ain|isam}}
#: {{usex|ain|Oroho ku-hotanukar kor, mokor wa '''an''' siri.|When I went to his place to see how he was doing, he seemed '''to be sleeping still'''.}}

====Conjugation====
{{ain-conj|1|an|okay}}

===Usage notes===
*As a verb, '''an''' cannot be negated by using any adverbs, such as '''somo'''. Instead, its [[antonym]]/[[complementary]] verb, [[isam]], should be used.
#: {{usex|ain|K-askepeci pisno sine am '''an'''. → K-askepeci pisno tu am '''isam'''.|Each one of my fingers '''have''' one nail. → Each one of my fingers '''don’t have''' two nails.}}

===Particle===
{{ain-verb|l|{{ain-kana-conv|アン}}}}

# {{lb|ain|emphatic}} A final particle used to emphasize or reinforce a statement; equivalent to Japanese [[よ]].
#: {{syn|ain|wa}}
#: {{usex|ain|Poronno opotuye okake, k-askepeci arka humi '''an'''.|My fingers '''really''' hurt after typing a lot.}}
# (''When before nouns'') Some, any, an [[undefined]] or [[unknown]] quantity of.
#: {{usex|ain|'''An''' cikoykip kotan peka anukar.|'''Some''' animals were seen in the village.}}

===Conjunction===
{{ain-verb|l|{{ain-kana-conv|アン}}}}

# (''When used with {{m|ain|kusu}}'') Thanks to, due to, using (something).
#: {{usex|ain|[[Ikaoykikur]] '''an kusu''', ku-pirka humi.|Thanks to the doctor, I feel better.}}

